Subject: [PATCH] k60: let a 540-byte 802.11 association event reach the daemon

kev_post_msg_internal copied every descriptor into one small mbuf and refused
anything over MLEN, so on the 27 line a join result is dropped with EMSGSIZE
before it reaches the daemon: the 24A446 association event carries a 540-byte
result structure (pong_assoc_event27). Give the IEEE80211 class a cluster mbuf
and check each descriptor against the limit the message really has.

Ported from UniXNU-sheng patches/xnu-12377/sheng-wifi-association-event.patch
(BSD-2-Clause-Patent, UniXNU contributors). The surrounding code is identical in
xnu ac9718f, so only the hunk offsets move.
Co-authored-by: UniXNU-sheng contributors <noreply@unixnu.com>
---
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_event.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_event.c
@@ -8913,22 +8913,21 @@
 	}
 #endif /* SKYWALK && XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX */
 
-	/* Verify the message is small enough to fit in one mbuf w/o cluster */
+	/* iPadOS 27 association events carry a 540-byte result structure. */
+	u_int32_t maximum = event_msg->vendor_code == KEV_VENDOR_APPLE &&
+	    event_msg->kev_class == KEV_IEEE80211_CLASS ? MCLBYTES : MLEN;
 	total_size = KEV_MSG_HEADER_SIZE;
-
 	for (i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
 		if (event_msg->dv[i].data_length == 0) {
 			break;
 		}
+		if (event_msg->dv[i].data_length > maximum - total_size) {
+			os_atomic_inc(&kevtstat.kes_toobig, relaxed);
+			return EMSGSIZE;
+		}
 		total_size += event_msg->dv[i].data_length;
 	}
-
-	if (total_size > MLEN) {
-		os_atomic_inc(&kevtstat.kes_toobig, relaxed);
-		return EMSGSIZE;
-	}
-
-	m = m_get(wait, MT_DATA);
+	m = total_size > MLEN ? m_getcl(wait, MT_DATA, 0) : m_get(wait, MT_DATA);
 	if (m == 0) {
 		os_atomic_inc(&kevtstat.kes_nomem, relaxed);
 		return ENOMEM;
